# Normalize line endings so a Windows checkout (git core.autocrlf=true) can't
# corrupt shell-script shebangs. A CRLF `#!/bin/sh\r` makes the kernel look for
# an interpreter literally named "/bin/sh\r", producing the Docker startup error
# "exec /usr/local/bin/entrypoint.sh: no such file or directory" (issues #150, #77).
* text=auto

# Shell scripts must stay LF on every platform (run by sh/bash, incl. in Docker).
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf
entrypoint.sh text eol=lf
docker/entrypoint.sh text eol=lf

# Windows-native scripts stay CRLF.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Vendored third-party bundles in static/lib/ are published minified artifacts
# and must stay byte-identical to what npm ships — stripping trailing whitespace
# to satisfy `git diff --check` would desync them from the upstream release. Turn
# the whitespace check off for that tree instead, and keep the bundles out of
# GitHub's language statistics.
#
# `-text` is the half this line was missing until `B362`, and it was missing on
# the side that matters. The rule above says these files must stay byte-identical
# to what upstream ships; without `-text` they resolved to `text: auto`, so on any
# clone with `core.autocrlf=true` — the Git for Windows default — git rewrote
# every LF to CRLF **on checkout**. Measured 2026-09-16 on the deployment host:
# **twelve of the thirty-eight files under `static/lib/` differed from their own
# git blobs**, `git status` reported the tree clean, and stripping the carriage
# returns reproduced each blob hash exactly. That working tree is the Docker
# build context, so the image was being built from bytes the repository does not
# contain. Nothing broke — JavaScript and CSS tolerate CRLF — which is precisely
# why it went unnoticed, and why an SRI hash or `check-vendored-versions.py`
# would have failed on that host and passed on Linux for the same commit.
static/lib/** -text -whitespace linguist-vendored

# Binary assets — never normalize.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf  binary
*.ico  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
# Pyodide (`P16-07`). `* text=auto` decides by content heuristic, which is a
# guess, and this repository has already shipped a CRLF corruption bug from a
# Windows checkout (issues #150, #77). A mangled 10 MB `.wasm` fails at
# instantiate with nothing useful on screen, so these are stated, not guessed.
*.wasm binary
*.zip  binary
